3. TRAINING METHODOLOGY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
  Primary loss : MultipleNegativesRankingLoss (MNRL)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Mechanism:
    For a batch of (query_i, positive_i) pairs, MNRL treats
    all positive_j (j ≠ i) as negatives for query_i.
    
    Objective: maximise cosine similarity of (q_i, pos_i)
               while minimising similarity of (q_i, pos_j≠i).

    Loss = -log [ exp(sim(q, pos) / τ) /
                  Σ_j exp(sim(q, pos_j) / τ) ]
    
    where τ = 1/scale = 1/20 = 0.05  (temperature).

  Effective negatives per sample: batch_size − 1 = 15
  
  Ablation loss: TripletLoss
    Loss = max(0, d(a,p) − d(a,n) + margin)
    margin = 0.5, distance = cosine
  
  Training config:
    Epochs        : 3  (MNRL),  2 (TripletLoss)
    Batch size    : 16
    Learning rate : 2e-5  (AdamW)
    Warmup ratio  : 10%
    Scheduler     : Linear warmup + linear decay

